# The dev server's secrets: copy to secrets.dev-server.env in the repo root
# (git-ignored), which every deploy uploads as secrets.env for the unit to
# load (docs/dev-server.md). JWT_SECRET is required: without it, or with it
# empty or "replace-me", the app refuses to boot. Without the MAILER_*
# lines it boots on the placeholders in config/dev-server.yaml, and mail
# fails to send.
#
# JWT_SECRET: the dev server's own, never staging's or production's. Base64,
# as Loco decodes it before signing; 64 bytes, as RFC 7518 asks of an
# HS512 key, Loco's. docs/dev-server.md's line adds one, made with
# `openssl rand -base64 64 | tr -d '\n'`.
# JWT_SECRET=

# Mail, only when the dev server should send real mail: all four together.
# Host on 587 with STARTTLS (465 needs MAILER_PORT=465 and `tls: implicit`
# in the config); an app password, never the account's; the sender as
# "Name <address>", in double quotes, on the account's address or domain
# (details in docs/production.md).
# MAILER_HOST=
# MAILER_USER=
# MAILER_PASSWORD=
# MAILER_FROM="App <noreply@dev.example.com>"
